A||N||10||CoolJoe12||Need more Power for my 2.5||||9||
Z||000000||CoolJoe12||01-18-2000||08:12 PM||||you guys got any ideas for my 88 coupe with a 2.5l with 75thousand miles on it it has in hte last 2 thouhsande mile had new exhaust put on it and a new head gasket.  I was woundering what would be the best route to get gt pertformance for about 1000 bucks I don't want to go the nitro route because for one nobody in town sells the stuff and two I don't feel comfortable with all the extra wear it will put on my engine.  I open to other sugestions <P>Also wounder what you guys think the best color would be to paint my car it has tan interior. right now I'm beetween blue and forest green.||||reg||9
Z||000001||862M4inCA||01-18-2000||08:19 PM||||I too have a 2.5 and am currently not aware of much in the way of modification aside from perhaps selling that one, and buying a V6. However you MIGHT be able to grab a super chip for a little added power, but even then I think you'd be happier with a V6. As for the paint. I would go with a medium metallic blue. I was thinking about going with that for mine which is currently red/gray but I think I may just go ahead and stick with the red.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||01-18-2000||08:46 PM||||A V6 is a definite improvement! If you're going to stick with the four, here's what I did. K&N air filter, removed the cat. convertor, a good tune up with Splitfire plugs, and installed the Ultimate Motor Mount from Fiero Store (dogbone). With 115K, it's runs very strong! My mechanic did some adjustment to the automatic trans so is shifts nice and firm at a higher RPM. The next step for me is to install the 58K mile Formula V6 engine I've got sitting in my garage!||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolJoe12||01-18-2000||08:52 PM||||yeah I thought of that but one major problem stopping what ever work I do would have to be a weekend job because being a high school student I have no other car to drive  and my dad who by the way is very good with cars is busy with his restoration of his 65 vette, (I would love to have about 5 grand to put in my car to blow the pants off this car for a 1/5th of the price.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fotofrank||01-19-2000||01:18 PM||||I have a 1984 2.5 and did the following. Removed the rain block behind the air intake,made a scoop instead of the intake grill,installed anMSD GM Blaster coil and MSD6A ignition. I had Bosch platanum plugs but changed to Champion steel when I installed the MSD stuff. The car seems stronger but still needs help. The next thing on the list is the Holley 500-1 TBI.<BR>I'm hoping the new TBI improves the power curve . Has anyone tried the Holley 500-1 TBI and did it improve preformance? <BR>Soomthing else you could try(also on my list) is a good valve job. Good luck and let us know what you do and the result of your mods.||||reg||10
Z||000006||DRH||01-19-2000||01:45 PM||||I would think you could sell your car. Take that money plus your $1000 and get a comparable V6 car. <B>Instant</B> V6 performance... Plus you still have room for more improvement. With the 4 I'm not sure you could get V6 performance for $1000. Even if you did, you would probably be pretty much maxed out on what the 4 will do (at least reliably, 2.5 is not known for strength).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||86SE||01-19-2000||04:35 PM||||Do what I did, get a 2.8L (or bigger) V-6, a K&N air filter, take out the cat. convertor, then buy a super chip and drill out the restrictons on the exhaust manifolds, and buy an power pully from the fiero store to pick up a a total of 15+ HP||||reg||14
Z||000008||theogre||01-19-2000||07:25 PM||||The is little you can do to the 87+ 4 cyl.<P>Accell makes better coils, but if yours are good then these are of limited benefit. If you opt for the MSD box then you might want these too, but don't be suprised if you get next to nothing in measurable power increase.<P>MSD makes an addon to the coil controller. It is an addon, it doesn't replace the controller. Presently I believe installation requires cutting the harness. ((MSD was working on a plug and play harness for it.))<P>There are no after market PROMs for the ECM. The Holley TBI upgrade is not compatible with 87+ motors.<P>There are some things you could maybe do, but your return on investment will likely be small. This motor already has a roller lifter cam. Fully electronic ignition. A better TBI unit and intake.||||reg||1
Z||000009||CoolJoe12||01-19-2000||10:49 PM||||yeah the main problem is that GTs for a teen have twice the insurance 1200 for the lowest coverage here is what I think I want to do<BR>put headers on it and a the holly TBI with a ram air kit I saw on the internet I already have the v6 exhaust istalled on it so I have a nice free flowing exhaust also do any of you know a engine swap place in the mid west area the  closer to michigan the better I may be able to get 2000 together for a swap.||||reg||1
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||01-20-2000||01:46 AM||||On my 87 coupe I too can vouch for the replacement of the rain catcher with a straight tube and the K&N Filter. The big difference came with replacing that joke of an exhaust manifold with one from Hooker,(the only one I know of) It was a Hooker Super Competition Tri-Y header. Putting this next to the stock exhaust set up is a real joke.<P>Problems I had with it though:<P>When I put it on at 153,000 miles without the Cat ( a BIG no-no here in CA) the improved flow proved too much for my old stock muffler and it blew a hole through it. The Dynomax muffler I had put on was a perfect replacement!<P>Pipe comes REAL close to the starter solenoid.<P>It needed to be rewelded at one of the Ys after a while.<P>But it brought that 4 banger to life! No I couldn't beat the V6s but I sure could stay up with them and on road trips when they were stopping to give their thirsty beasts a drink I was just topping off my tank!||||reg||1
Z||000011||GT Bastard||01-20-2000||03:23 AM||||My Gt's insurance was the same as my 4-bangers insurance, and the Gt is newer.  I'm going through Progressive.||||reg||1
